// The game clock and the anchors that pin every calendar to day 0 (GDD §3, ADR-0009).
//
// Times are minutes since the midnight that opens the game day. A day runs
// 05:00 → 01:00, so `dayEndMinute` is past 24:00 (1500 = 01:00 the next morning).
// At 10 sim ticks per second (ARCHITECTURE §3.1), 7 ticks per game minute is the
// GDD's "1 game-minute = 0.7 real s", which makes a day ~14 real minutes.
//
// `arrival` is day 0, a design choice: 1 Juli 2026, in the kemarau, so the kalen is dry
// when the player arrives. It must be a date the scaled calendar shows (the 1st always
// is). Day 0's weekday and pasaran are the real ones for that date — Rabu Wage — and
// then each advances one per game day.
//
// `jawa`: the Javanese year is the Hijri year + 512 (Sultan Agung aligned 1 Sura 1555
// with 1 Muharram 1043), and 1956 was an Alip year, so 1959 is Je and 1960 is Dal.
// verified: false — against a published Javanese almanac (primbon / kalender Jawa).
{
  ticksPerMinute: 7,
  dayStartMinute: 300,
  dayEndMinute: 1500,
  arrival: { year: 2026, month: 7, day: 1 },
  jawa: { hijriYearOffset: 512, alipYear: 1956 },
}
